In addition to the Agresti books already mentioned (which are good) there are

Goodman, L. (1984)  The analysis of cross classified data having ordered 
categories.  Harvard U. P

Cliff, N. (1996).  Ordinal methods for behavioral data analysis.  Lawrence 
Erlbaum Assoc.

and

Clogg, C. and Shihadeh, E. (1994) Statistical models for ordinal variables. 
Sage.

The first is a collection of Goodman's papers.  He has written and thought a 
LOT about this topic.

The second is a, to my mind, somewhat simplistic approach recommending using 
some (relatively) standard nonparametric procedures in novel ways.

The last is a highly innovative approach, which appears to me to be very 
useful.  I would love if someone wrote some S-Plus programs to do these 
analyses, my skills are not up to it.

You might also want to look for articles by Don Hedeker.

