I have found the GUI to be tolerable when displaying on the host that 
is running it.

In contrast, when displaying remotely, I have found it to be 
unacceptably slow and nearly un-readable. The release notes have a 
section titled "Java Display Issues." You should read them if you 
haven't already. Here's a quote: "When using a remote display, Java 
renders the display on the server and then ships a bitmap of the 
application region to the remote display." Another quote: "...network 
delays can sometimes severely degrade the performance of a Java 
application displayed remotely from the server where it is generated."

